{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets","id":186259,"title":"Clarifying uses for Embeded Gadgets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-02T06:58:53-07:00","id":186259,"title":"Clarifying uses for Embeded Gadgets","content":"I am still not entirely sure why Demons would create vanilla Embeded gadgets, considering the hefty cost in loss of Willpower dots. Exploit gadgets, I get - no compromise rolls is a significant feature. The new-fangled types - Lambdas, Near-fields, Overclocked, Form - again there are obvious advantages. But simple vanilla Embed gadgets from the core book - not so much.<br /> <br /> The alleged advantages for gadgets are:<br /> 1. No compromise rolls. But most embeds don't cause compromise rolls anyway<br /> 2. Blending in. But, again, most embeds are pretty subtle to warrant the expenditure of time and willpower dots to offer any kind of justifiable advantage<br /> 3. Reliability. But, unless the trigger is specifically chosen to not involve any rolls, activating a Gadget still requires a roll.<br /> 4. Use in pacts and for general bargaining. But a pact is able to manifest whatever the pactee asks out of thin air. Why would a demon expend valuable resources and willpower when Primum can do it much more easily? Yes, there are limits to what a pact can grant but still I am struggling to imagine a mortal agonizing over &quot;I could give away all my illnesses, abusive relationships etc ... OR I can have a lighter that creates a loud bang&quot;...<br /> 5. Equipping your cultists.<br /> <br /> So it seems to me that Embed gadgets are only useful if:<br /> 1. They have a non-roll trigger<br /> 2. As a roll-converter of some sort (i.e. If you'd rather roll Dexterity+Academics on a book instead of Manipulation+Expression on Trivia, for example)<br /> 3. As equipment for your cult<br /> 4. Trading between demons for Embeds you don't know<br /> <br /> Still useful, I suppose, but it seems to me more limited than the core book implies. Is that a fair assessment or am I missing obvious applications?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T11:09:40-07:00","id":186423,"title":"","content":"Firstly, that assessment as it turns out depends highly on the embed in question.<br /> <br /> Other advantages include: The ability to create an effect that is not normally the purview of the Embed itself, but is close to it. Example: A silk shirt embedded with Just Bruised. It still looks like a silk shirt, but it might provide ballistic armour or defense when worn.<br /> <br /> Embedded Gadgets do not require the demon to recharge them like Exploited gadgets do. Once you've expended the aether, you've got your new toy.<br /> <br /> An Embedded Gadget might be able to activate itself under certain condition, such as: &quot;Wearer is shot.&quot; Meaning that those nasty surprise rounds aren't such a problem anymore when your Just Bruised shirt has your back.<br /> <br /> Embedded Gadgets could be used to set up traps in your home to protect you from God-Machine interference such as sneaky cultists, police or angels. <i>Example: </i><i>The demon installs Combustion into the window-frames or doors of the sensitive areas of their home so that anyone whom climbs into them causes a house-fire. The demon then knows that there is a good chance that any evidence of their demonic self has been destroyed and they can then seek refuge in a bug-out cover until things blow over.</i><br /> <br /> Embedded Gadgets could be used to set up defenses in your home, rather than just traps. <i>Example: (I can't take the credit for this one!) The demon installs Tools into Toys in the locks surrounding a sensitive area making them nigh-impossible for mundane characters to pick.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T13:19:13-07:00","id":186463,"title":"","content":"Several thoughts. First is? If its in an embedded object, you don't need to spend time activating the embed, then doing whatever. Take the example of the knife with Hush. Normally, you'd need to activate the Embed, then attack. With the knife, you have the knife and no sound happens, no activation time required.<br /> <br /> Second thought is what Dolly said - the gadget may not have anything to do with the normal use of the Embed. Using the knife again, but lets put Merciless Gunman in it instead. Normally, you can't use it with something other than a gun. Perhaps as a gadget, it would? Benefits of the embed, but in a different way not possible before.<br /> <br /> Third is that you can give them out, trade them around to demons and stigmatics who don't know the Embed. Or perhaps for a pact fulfillment, instead of doing something yourself.<br /> <br /> Fourth idea that comes to mind is that gadgets are potentially persistently turned on. So, if you want an effect that's always running without conscious effort on your part? Take... backdrop. Good way to avoid being ambushed with a gun. Would be awesome for bodyguard work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T16:19:52-07:00","id":186605,"title":"","content":"Also, because a lot of embedded gadgets would be just plain cool to have. I can think of so many things I want to embed with Knockout Punch it's not funny (except that many of them would be funny, like a white glove for challenging people to duels).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T01:59:46-07:00","id":186936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=186423#post186423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Firstly, that assessment as it turns out depends highly on the embed in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. But I am thinking more general guidelines. The reason is that I have players who are playing freshly-fallen demons bu the players are both very risk averse and not very familiar with the rules yet. So they have bought into the paranoia setting very well but it's taking some effort to convince them to spend resources like willpower and aether because everything appears scarce to them. In due time. as they learn more about how the rules and the setting work, that will change but right now &quot;it's cool&quot; definitely does not cut it with them if they have to lose a dot of willpower for no obvious gain. Similarly, because they only know like 3-4 embeds the nuances that gadgets may work better with some embeds than others are harder to appreciate. Hence the &quot;search&quot; for general guidelines and motivations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other advantages include: The ability to create an effect that is not normally the purview of the Embed itself, but is close to it. Example: A silk shirt embedded with Just Bruised. It still looks like a silk shirt, but it might provide ballistic armour or defense when worn. </div> </div> </div>Is that true though? My understanding was that (with possible exceptions of near-fields and overclocking) a gadget can *only* do what an Embed can do but in a narrower sense. I think the shirt example you gave is more an example of &quot;persistency&quot; that MCN mentions rather than an example of extending the functionality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Embedded Gadgets do not require the demon to recharge them like Exploited gadgets do. Once you've expended the aether, you've got your new toy. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's an advantage of an Embedded Gadget over and Exploited Gadget where as I am looking for advantages of Embedded Gadgets over their underlying Embeds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An Embedded Gadget might be able to activate itself under certain condition, such as: &quot;Wearer is shot.&quot; Meaning that those nasty surprise rounds aren't such a problem anymore when your Just Bruised shirt has your back.<br /> <br /> Embedded Gadgets could be used to set up traps in your home to protect you from God-Machine interference such as sneaky cultists, police or angels. <i>Example: </i><i>The demon installs Combustion into the window-frames or doors of the sensitive areas of their home so that anyone whom climbs into them causes a house-fire. The demon then knows that there is a good chance that any evidence of their demonic self has been destroyed and they can then seek refuge in a bug-out cover until things blow over.</i><br /> <br /> Embedded Gadgets could be used to set up defenses in your home, rather than just traps. <i>Example: (I can't take the credit for this one!) The demon installs Tools into Toys in the locks surrounding a sensitive area making them nigh-impossible for mundane characters to pick.</i> </div> </div> </div>Yes! This is definition a very important application that I had missed, thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If its in an embedded object, you don't need to spend time activating the embed, then doing whatever. Take the example of the knife with Hush. Normally, you'd need to activate the Embed, then attack. With the knife, you have the knife and no sound happens, no activation time required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes. I hadn't thought about that as we haven't had much combat. So yeah where &quot;turns&quot; are important, that's an issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second thought is what Dolly said - the gadget may not have anything to do with the normal use of the Embed. Using the knife again, but lets put Merciless Gunman in it instead. Normally, you can't use it with something other than a gun. Perhaps as a gadget, it would? Benefits of the embed, but in a different way not possible before. </div> </div> </div>Again, i would question that... That's not how I am reading the rules, personally.. In this specific example I would say that a gun has no &quot;sympathetic resonance&quot; (FoH-p.150) with Merciless Gunmen. To me it goes against the spirit of the rules to let a normal gadget to do something the underlying embed could not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third is that you can give them out, trade them around to demons and stigmatics who don't know the Embed. Or perhaps for a pact fulfillment, instead of doing something yourself. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this use I was aware of but I am not sure how effective it is... When a demon enters into a pact he doesn't have to do anything itself. Its side of the pact is fullfilled by Primum &quot;magic&quot;. It's not like Changeling pledges where you actually have to go and do something. So why would a Demon give out something that is actually a loss to itself when it could just have Primum do it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fourth idea that comes to mind is that gadgets are potentially persistently turned on. So, if you want an effect that's always running without conscious effort on your part? </div> </div> </div>Yes, this I like!<br /> <br /> Thank you, lot's of good stuff here! So to my list above I can also now add:<br /> <br /> Vanilla Embedded Gadgets are also useful if:<br /> 5. You want the Embed effect to be delayed, triggered or otherwise physically removed from where you are<br /> 6. You want the Embed effect to be persistent or otherwise not require an Instant action<br /> <br /> I am still not sold on how useful gadgets would be for Pacts though... And am not really convinced that you should be allowed to expand the functionality of Embeds by installing them<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T05:27:27-07:00","id":186982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=186936#post186936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And am not really convinced that you should be allowed to expand the functionality of Embeds by installing them</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what the entire section on &quot;Near Field Effects&quot; (P149) is about in its entirety - covering effects that should logically come from an embed but aren't covered specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am still not sold on how useful gadgets would be for Pacts though </div> </div> </div>Use something like one-shots to get someone hooked on something. Get a one-shot embed with download knowledge that gives you dots in Science or something, for example. &quot;Hey, this thing will help you become a genius, for a short time.&quot; Imagine how addictive it would be - use this device, suddenly feel smart. Imagine how the withdrawal would feel! So, you get them on a temporary pact - they come back for bigger and better pacts for better bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T19:16:58-07:00","id":187575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=186423#post186423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embedded Gadgets could be used to set up defenses in your home, rather than just traps. <i>Example: (I can't take the credit for this one!) The demon installs Tools into Toys in the locks surrounding a sensitive area making them nigh-impossible for mundane characters to pick.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have spend it on a few strong points or else you're going to be guzzling Permanent Willpower. Maybe you could install it into your house keys (ex: any door locked by this key becomes unpickable, gadget limitation: only works on locks matching the key) or into the locks as a one-time gadget using Aether instead of Permanent Willpower (giving the additional benefit of alerting you that someone has <i>tried</i> to pick the locks when you next inspect the gadgets and find it to no longer be a gadget, hmmm... I think I like that better)<br /> <br /> Alternately, try installing something nasty on your home security system. Try... say Deafen ( the blaring alarm leaves the intruders disoriented), Fire Alarm (intruders hearing the alarm becomes disoriented and confused) Trust No One (the Reservoir Dogs Gadget. Anyone hearing that bank alarm is convinced that they were set up by their partners/employers/family. If they're all armed... I'm sure you can figure out where that's going) or Tag And Release (any one tripping the alarm is now tracked) and you have one gadget protecting your entire premises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","user":"Agentwestmer","date":". 07-03-2014, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T06:24:39-07:00","id":187894,"title":"","content":"Agentwestmer has the right of it. You have to be careful when taking that approach, but it can be done. (I particularly like the idea of the keys.)<br /> <br /> The Just Bruised Embed reduces the incoming damage, on a success, to 1. Where as the shirt would either provide armour or defense. While the effect is similar, it is not the same, and is weaker than that of the embed. So it would be able to provide that benefit.<br /> <br /> Merciless Gunman in a bladed weapon is a bit more debatable. A similar argument came up with my players: Could Hellfire be installed on a sword to change it's damage type from L to A? This, I believe, is up to the storyteller and whether or not they believe the power and the implement are not resonant enough with one another.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think they are within reason as both are weapons and it depends entirely on the derived effect. I think an exploited techno-sword (or even lightsaber) is bizarre enough a weapon and hard enough to hide that the pay-off for converting its damage type to aggravated isn't a bit deal. Besides, how else can you make a Seraph's flaming sword? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T13:29:37-07:00","id":188208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=186982#post186982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what the entire section on &quot;Near Field Effects&quot; (P149) is about in its entirety - covering effects that should logically come from an embed but aren't covered specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, you have a point I suppose. I should clarify what I meant. The way I understand Near-Field gadgets is that they allow you to negotiate with the Storyteller to deviate from the *mechanical/game rules* description of the Embed provided it is consistent with the *flavour/technognostic* interpretation of what physical laws that Embed describes. From the in-character point of view, I guess this means that demon, who knows a particular law of the universe, may not immediately realise all of its applications but by experimenting with gadgets it expands its knowledge. Much like a physicist may know laws of optics, which allow him to make refraction prisms. But by playing around with double-slit experiments the physicist may discover the particle-wave duality and now understand the quantum mechanical implications of the optics laws he already knew. So, I guess, yes in that sense you are right - one of the uses of gadgets is to experiment with the laws of the universe and discover alternative applications.<br /> <br /> However, I would argue that once you succeed in making a near-field gadget you've succeeded in your experiment, you've gained new understanding of that particular physical law. Therefore, now whenever you use the underlying Embed you can use it for its near-field effect as well as it's original effect. In that sense, gadgets still stay within the original restriction of not doing anything the underlying Embed can't do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Use something like one-shots to get someone hooked on something. Get a one-shot embed with download knowledge that gives you dots in Science or something, for example. &quot;Hey, this thing will help you become a genius, for a short time.&quot; Imagine how addictive it would be - use this device, suddenly feel smart. Imagine how the withdrawal would feel! So, you get them on a temporary pact - they come back for bigger and better pacts for better bonuses. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but why is it something worth a willpower dot (which you still need to make one-shots) if you could just make a day-long duration pact for a greater asset (like loads of points in Resources, for example) which doesn't cost you anything and achieves the same &quot;hooking up&quot; effect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T18:21:30-07:00","id":188358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I would argue that once you succeed in making a near-field gadget you've succeeded in your experiment, you've gained new understanding of that particular physical law. Therefore, now whenever you use the underlying Embed you can use it for its near-field effect as well as it's original effect. In that sense, gadgets still stay within the original restriction of not doing anything the underlying Embed can't do. </div> </div> </div>The problem is: This isn't true by RAW and certainly arguably even RAI. One of the single largest advantages of gadgets, prior to Flowers of Hell, as stated by the book was a demon's ability to use a physical object to alter his ability <i>within that gadget. </i>If a Near-Field gadget effect allows you to cast that effect as the Embed, then there is no point in gadgets as permanent objects - completely negating their cost of willpower and takes away their intended purpose as &quot;magical, enchanted items&quot; and simply makes them into &quot;practice my embeds to bend the rules&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T06:03:58-07:00","id":188664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=188358#post188358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is: This isn't true by RAW and certainly arguably even RAI. One of the single largest advantages of gadgets, prior to Flowers of Hell, as stated by the book was a demon's ability to use a physical object to alter his ability <i>within that gadget. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean to come across as being confrontational, but do you mind directing me to a citation on this? All of my argumentation above comes precisely from an understanding that in RAW that is not the case (RAI may vary of course).<br /> <br /> All I can find in the core book is:<br /> <br /> p.25: &quot; Gadget: an object with an Embed Installed into it that can be used by anyone&quot;<br /> p.187, 1 column: &quot; a demon can imbue<b> specific aspects of Embeds</b> and Exploits into a physical object, altering its fundamental structure and granting it supernatural properties.&quot;<br /> p.187, 2 column: &quot; It is now a supernatural tool, instilled with magical properties <b>derived from the Installed Embed</b>.&quot;<br /> ibid. :&quot; They always have a <b>specific effect related to the Embed from which they are derived</b>.&quot;<br /> p.188, 2 column: &quot; Installation cannot convey the full effect of an Embed or Exploit. Gadgets offset portability and reliability with inflexible single-function usage that represents <b>only a portion of the Embed</b>\u2019s or Exploit\u2019s potential. &quot;<br /> ibid: &quot; If a gadget seems right, go with it, even if it changes the assumptions of the Embed/Exploit slightly. &quot;<br /> <br /> And that's about it... Apart from the last line nothing suggests to me that an Embedded Gadget can go outside the purview of the underlying Embed. The last line, to me, says that you can (slightly) change the assumptions of the Embed itself. i.e. you decide that the Embed itself works slightly differently from its official write-up and that allows you to make a Gadget that &quot;seems right&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a Near-Field gadget effect allows you to cast that effect as the Embed, then there is no point in gadgets as permanent objects - completely negating their cost of willpower and takes away their intended purpose as &quot;magical, enchanted items&quot; and simply makes them into &quot;practice my embeds to bend the rules&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, indeed. That concern was precisely the reason for this topic as I couldn't see the point of creating these objects at that cost. But the above discussion suggests that in fact there are a number of uses apart from &quot;practice my embeds to bend the rules&quot; that benefit from gadgets being permanent objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:19:14-07:00","id":188821,"title":"","content":"p. 187 &quot;A Corporate ID Badge Installed with Unperson (p. 147) that makes it difficult to recall the wearer\u2019s identity.&quot;<br /> Unperson is an offensive embed to be used on a target to remove their identity. This is psychic paper that stops you remembering who flashed it. Is it within the purview of the original embed? No. Not unless you unperson every single person you meet that is in an official position and suffer the eyes of the God-Machine upon you for collapsing social structures. It is an example of a near-field gadget. Your suggestion is that they should be able to mimic that effect with Unperson, but the RAW doesn't support that. Certainly, and much like some finding the Dramatic Failure of certain embeds and exploits more favorable than their success conditions, you could always make a new Embed to support that functionality - indeed the character would then have to pay 2 experience. But should they be able to just flash a badge and the person forgets them because they've made that gadget? I don't think so.<br /> <br /> The last line you quoted is of the biggest important as it is later expounded upon as &quot;Near-Field&quot; gadgets in Flowers of Hell. In the end, I guess, a storyteller has to ask themselves what is your definition of &quot;slightly&quot;. Their definition of slightly seems interesting as certainly you could hypothetically use Unperson on yourself to make everyone forget you - however dangerous that might be - but the base assumption of the Embed is offensive. Or so it is in my reading? Also, not finding you confrontational. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T01:46:46-07:00","id":189253,"title":"","content":"Gadgets can be given away. Give your buddy a merciless gunman pistol and you've doubled the effectiveness of your embed in a firefight, a pretty nice deal for just one willpower point. For five points you have your own demonically powered SWAT unit. I don't know about you, but having a group of people who can quickly make you the only living person in the room hardly seems useless. <br /> <br /> Gadgets can change the dice pool depending on the form of the gadget. That knife of hushing certainly isn't shutting people up with a brawl roll. <br /> <br /> And of course there are near field and lambda gadgets.<br /> <br /> As for allowing one to essentially learn a new free embed or exploit by making a near field effect, by that logic all demons ought to be able to overclock their powers because gadgets can do that. By that logic making a lambda gadget would allow a demon to combine their powers. By that logic demons can change their dice pools on embeds and exploits because demons can do that when they make gadgets. <br /> <br /> You are free to do whatever you like in your own games, but that sounds like a big can of worms to me. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:40:13-07:00","id":189450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=188821#post188821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">p. 187 &quot;A Corporate ID Badge Installed with Unperson (p. 147) that makes it difficult to recall the wearer\u2019s identity.&quot;<br /> Unperson is an offensive embed to be used on a target to remove their identity. This is psychic paper that stops you remembering who flashed it. Is it within the purview of the original embed? No. Not unless you unperson every single person you meet that is in an official position and suffer the eyes of the God-Machine upon you for collapsing social structures. It is an example of a near-field gadget. Your suggestion is that they should be able to mimic that effect with Unperson, but the RAW doesn't support that. Certainly, and much like some finding the Dramatic Failure of certain embeds and exploits more favorable than their success conditions, you could always make a new Embed to support that functionality - indeed the character would then have to pay 2 experience. But should they be able to just flash a badge and the person forgets them because they've made that gadget? I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify what I mean by &quot;purview&quot;.. The flavour of the embed is that it is an underlying law of the universe. The write-up of an Embed includes a brief summary of what that &quot;law&quot; is and gives the game-rules implementation for a typical use. Necessarily, the rulebook cannot attempt to cover every consequences of that &quot;law&quot; in the short and concise write up. My understanding of the gadget restriction on using only a part of the Embed's function is that it refers to the &quot;fluff&quot;, not the rules text. According to that interpretation, the ID badge is not within the purview of the typical offensive rules-write up given in the book but it is, in my opinion, within the purview of the &quot;fluff&quot;. Unperson write up states &quot;a demon with the right expertise can force a person into a kind of \u201cidentity blackout\u201d for a short time, making her unrecognizable and unable to identify herself.&quot; The rules for gadgets permit only a partial functionality to be installed. Thus the ID badge installs the &quot;making her unrecognizable&quot; part but not the &quot;unable to identify herself&quot; part.<br /> <br /> By that reading, I would indeed consider allowing such a use of Unperson once the near-field gadget is created. Now, yes, of course - there is a risk of the slippery slope scenario here. you can certainly keep pushing the bounds of the Embed effect too much. But I would say there are three safe-guards for that: 1) the spirit of what the Embed represents, 2) the consent of the story-teller to create a near-field effect and 3) the fact that, as you say, once the effect is so far removed from the original Embed as to be a new Embed the ST can require 2 XP.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for allowing one to essentially learn a new free embed or exploit by making a near field effect, by that logic all demons ought to be able to overclock their powers because gadgets can do that. By that logic making a lambda gadget would allow a demon to combine their powers. </div> </div> </div> </div>I don't immediately see a problem with that. Overclocking an Embed is essentially how a demon discovers Exploits. That's what Exploits (by flavour) are: Embeds that are forced with Aether. And I don't see any obvious restrictions to why a demon can't combine Embed effects - I have seen a number of such suggestions on these very forums.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By that logic demons can change their dice pools on embeds and exploits because demons can do that when they make gadgets. </div> </div> </div>This I think is different. The roll used to activate a gadget has nothing to do with the Embed, it's a property of the hardware. Thus it tells the demon nothing new about the laws of the universe; it wouldn't warrant any change to how the demon knows to use the underlying Embed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are free to do whatever you like in your own games, but that sounds like a big can of worms to me. </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, I am willing to concede that I am overthinking and overinterpreting the rules. And certainly I can see problems with my interpretation. But I still don't see how else to reconcile the proposal that gadgets can go beyond what an Embed can do with the explicit requirement that it represents &quot;only a portion of the Embed's potential&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T09:09:34-07:00","id":189469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/186259-clarifying-uses-for-embeded-gadgets?p=189450#post189450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify what I mean by &quot;purview&quot;.. The flavour of the embed is that it is an underlying law of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>So's chemistry, but that doesn't mean I can make diamonds just by having a fistful of pencil lead or fix nitrogen into soil without bacteria. You need the right technology.<br /> <br /> Mind, an Interlock to use a near-field effect of an Embed that you know might be a curious outcome, if tricky to balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T09:21:55-07:00","id":189479,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think I am confusing the issue by going on a tangent too much.<br /> <br /> The main question is: &quot;How do you reconcile the explicit requirement in the rules to only use a restricted part of an Embed when creating a gadget with the claim that a gadget can do things that an Embed cannot&quot;? What do the rules mean, then, when they say &quot;Installation cannot convey the full effect of an Embed or Exploit. Gadgets offset portability and reliability with inflexible single-function usage that represents <b>only a portion of the Embed</b>\u2019s or Exploit\u2019s potential.&quot;?<br /> <br /> What *is* the restriction?<br /> <br /> My own interpretations aside, my main problem at the moment is that I can't seem to reconcile the majority opinion in this thread with those words in the core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2108-genesis","name":"genesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T15:12:56-07:00","id":189667,"title":"","content":"When you use the Embed, you can use it with all the creativity that you can think of without modifying the actual effects.<br /> <br /> When you install the Embed into a Gadget, you can get effects beyond it's normal purview (Near-Field Effects) but at the cost of the versatility. Your Gadget accomplishes a cool, different effect or does it better than your dice might typically allow, but it only does so in that particular capacity, rather than the full options the original Embed might allow.<br /> <br /> So you could make a Near-Field Combustion Gadget that causes people's clothes to spontaneously combust. It's a near-field effect because the original Embed can't do it, but you can't use the Gadget to raise the flammability of everything else anymore. You'll have to use the Embed for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}